              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "If you’re still on stock Android…\n\nGoogle silently installs SafetyCore (on-device sensitive content scanning)\nand it reinstalls itself every time you try to remove it.\n\nThe community’s solution is simple and effective:\na placeholder APK with an absurdly high version number (2,000,000,000).\n\nOnce installed, Google can no longer overwrite it.\n1. Uninstall SafetyCore\n\n2. Install the placeholder\n\n3. Keep control of your device\n\nGitHub: https://t.co/enSZbjA2Ho\n\nEven blocking a Google component requires workarounds on stock Android.\n\nHave you tried it? Does it hold up over time for you?\n\n#Privacy #DeGoogle #Android #SafetyCore #DigitalSovereignty"
        },
        "paid_partnership": false,
        "possibly_sensitive": false,
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 2207,
